 <rdf:Description rdf:about=''
  xmlns:acdsee='http://ns.acdsee.com/iptc/1.0/'>
  <acdsee:caption>Slices through the computational domain of radial velocity relative to the stellar center as the hot convective plume rises. Positive velocities indicate outflow, while negative velocities inflow in this frame of reference. The upper panels slice through the stellar envelope in the xâ€“y plane. The lower panels show slices at a radius of 770 R                      âŠ™ at the same times. The hot fluid, initially located at (x, y) = ( + 335 R                      âŠ™, 0), begins rising and spreading over several hundred days as it breaks out of the stellar envelope.</acdsee:caption>
 </rdf:Description>

